<title>USA: Littlefield needs funds, sales.</title>
<headline>Littlefield needs funds, sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Littlefield, Adams &amp; Co, reporting a net loss amid an 85 percent drop in product sales in the second quarter, said Thursday it needed more funds or sales to remain in business.</p>
<p>&quot;Without the generation of additional sales or the procurement of additional funds through new borrowings ..., it is likely the company will not have sufficient cash flows to maintain itself after the 1997 third quarter,&quot; a company statement said.</p>
</text>
